// Title: Interactive AT Job
// Sigma ID: 60fc936d-2eb0-4543-8a13-911c750a1dfc
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: E.M. Anhaus (originally from Atomic Blue Detections, Endgame), oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-24 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: persistence, execution, privilege-escalation, T1053.002
// Description: Detects an interactive AT job, which may be used as a form of privilege escalation.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely (at.exe deprecated as of Windows 8)
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1053.002/T1053.002.md
//   - https://eqllib.readthedocs.io/en/latest/analytics/d8db43cf-ed52-4f5c-9fb3-c9a4b95a0b56.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_at_interactive_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\at.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "interactive"
